{"lines": ["In October 1955, the Joyita left Samoa for the Tokelau Islands, a trip of about two days.", "Her holds were lined with cork, which made her almost impossible to sink.", "She sailed with one engine broken, and twenty-five people aboard, including a doctor and two children.", "No distress call was ever heard.", "Planes searched nearly 100,000 square miles of ocean, and found nothing.", "Five weeks later, a merchant ship found her drifting, half under water, more than 600 miles off her route, with nobody aboard.", "Her radio was set to the distress channel, but a broken cable had been painted over, so it could only reach about two miles.", "Her clocks had stopped at 10:25, and the lights were switched on, so it probably happened at night.", "On deck lay a doctor's bag, with a stethoscope, a scalpel, and four blood-stained bandages.", "And just like on the Mary Celeste and the Deering, the navigation instruments were gone: her sextant, her chronometer, and her logbook too.", "The inquiry called the fate of the people aboard \"inexplicable.\"", "No trace of the twenty-five people has ever been found."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.5], ["October", 0.5, 0.55], ["1955,", 0.55, 1.68], ["the", 2.74, 2.88], ["Joyita", 2.88, 3.28], ["left", 3.28, 3.64], ["Samoa", 3.64, 3.94], ["for", 3.94, 4.4], ["the", 4.4, 4.52], ["Tokelau", 4.52, 5.04], ["Islands,", 5.04, 5.34], ["a", 5.92, 6.1], ["trip", 6.1, 6.3], ["of", 6.3, 6.58], ["about", 6.58, 6.82], ["two", 6.82, 7.12], ["days.", 7.12, 7.42], ["Her", 8.04, 8.16], ["holds", 8.16, 8.44], ["were", 8.44, 8.74], ["lined", 8.74, 9.0], ["with", 9.0, 9.32], ["cork,", 9.32, 9.66], ["which", 10.06, 10.22], ["made", 10.22, 10.42], ["her", 10.42, 10.62], ["almost", 10.62, 10.94], ["impossible", 10.94, 11.42], ["to", 11.42, 11.86], ["sink.", 11.86, 12.08], ["She", 12.66, 12.78], ["sailed", 12.78, 12.98], ["with", 12.98, 13.34], ["one", 13.34, 13.58], ["engine", 13.58, 13.96], ["broken,", 13.96, 14.3], ["and", 14.92, 15.02], ["twenty-five"